Edit an AI draft into a credible professional voice — learner brief
Fictional Northstar Services training material.
Approved fictional facts
F1 September budget USD 200,000. F2 actual USD 218,000; supplied variance USD 18,000 / 9%. F3 approved explanation USD 12,000 contractor extension and USD 6,000 travel. F4 forecast revision proposed, unapproved. F5 operations lead must confirm remaining contractor end date by September 25.
Original flawed draft
In these dynamic times, we remain committed to optimizing outcomes. September actual spending was USD 218,000 versus USD 200,000 budget. The USD 12,000 contractor extension and USD 6,000 travel explain the difference. The revised forecast is now approved. We hope operations can provide details when convenient.
Style
Direct opening; short paragraphs; respectful tone; no unexplained jargon.
Task
An accurate draft is too vague and ceremonial for Northstar's internal style.
Actions
	1	Highlight the unsupported statement separately from style problems.
	2	Ask AI for a revision using the style brief and only F1–F5.
	3	Compare the revision with the original and reject any new commitments.
	4	Cut filler and ensure the request remains visible.
	5	Explain one factual correction and three audience-related edits.
Output
Original draft; edited draft up to 150 words; factual repair; three style edits and their purpose.
